#!/bin/zsh
TMUX=/opt/homebrew/bin/tmux
[ -x "$TMUX" ] || TMUX=/usr/local/bin/tmux
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe3:1.1 C-u; sleep 1
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe3:1.1 "DROP the Firestore work entirely - V asked why we need it and the honest answer is we do not. The clips are in R2 and always were; Firestore was only ever for ground truth about which doctor was in which room, and your own roster analysis already showed that value collapsing - two doctors appear in more than one room on Saturday and eight of the nine staffed rooms hold more than one doctor, so a static single-valued doctor-room map cannot represent the day no matter what it contains. I was chasing a permission we do not need. Do not request a Firestore role and do not export a key. NEW TASK, and it is the one that matters. split-speaker found a doctor whose 3,247 seconds of speech comes from only 16 turns averaging about 200 seconds each, and earlier work flagged one claimed turn of 204 seconds and one unnamed turn of 266 seconds as near-certainly mis-segmented. INVESTIGATE THE SEGMENTER. Questions: how many turns across the whole corpus exceed 60 seconds, and what is the distribution - is this a handful of outliers or a systematic failure mode. For the long ones, what distinguishes them: a particular room, date, engine, window, chunk boundary, or a silence-threshold path. Does a 200-second turn contain one speaker or several - check whether diarization emitted it as a single segment or whether something downstream merged several. And the consequence I care most about: if a turn glues a doctor and a patient together, then any clinician_id attached to it is attached to mixed audio, which would corrupt both the speaker-ID measurement AND any enrolment harvested from it. Tell me whether the 957 named turns include any of these long ones and how many. CONSTRAINTS: read-only, no writes to anything, no transcript text, counts and ids and durations only. Neon HTTP driver - no sql.unsafe, timestamps come back as ISO strings. Report the distribution, the distinguishing feature if you find one, the single-versus-several verdict with how you established it, and the count of affected named turns. CAP 250 words."; sleep 2
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe3:1.1 Enter; sleep 2
$TMUX send-keys -t scribe3:1.1 Enter; sleep 1
echo sent
